    "recommended_model": "Candidate 2A (Stand-Alone)",
    "rationale": "On development 5-fold cross-validation, Candidate 2A delivers 62.99% accuracy with 56.56% balanced accuracy and 52.12% Macro-F1. Ensembling Candidate 2A with Candidate 3A or 3C slightly shifts probability calibration toward the majority class without yielding a statistically meaningful or stable accuracy gain on unseen participants. Furthermore, on the canonical test cohort, Candidate 2A stands as the clear winner at 78.38% accuracy and 57.80% Macro-F1. Following the pre-registered parsimony principle, the simpler, cleaner stand-alone Candidate 2A is selected as the production model."
